00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:06.309 align:start position:0%
in this rna-seq demo pipeline we will  learn how we can generate rna gene  expression tables from the raw rna  secrets  you will see a menu of areas of analysis  or data types that you can process in  the transcriptomic section on the upper  left there is a drop down on the right  side of the rna seq chip option  if you click on this drop down it will  show you three demo pipeline options the  first step in your analysis is to choose  a pipeline here we are choosing the rnsc  pipeline associated with the patient  derived xenograft project in this  project we have mainly two breast cancer  subtypes  that is estrogen receptor positive and  triple negative  to begin this pipeline click on demo  rna-seq pdx project  after you are done clicking you will get  the interface with the pipeline  after clicking the start you will get a  pop-up to load the input files by  clicking ok  since this is a demo pipeline the files  will be automatically uploaded  once you start your pipeline the next is  pre-processing of raw reads here we are  performing two pre-processing steps  removal of adapters and removal of pcr  duplicates  during the rna sequencing process  adapters are attached to the reads in  this pipeline the trimomatic module  remove those adapters when you click on  trimomatic option you will get a pop-up  with the details  all you need to do is just click ok  once the dramomatic step is completed  the next pre-processing step is pcr  clean which will get highlighted  in this pipeline the pcr clean module  removes those adapters  once you pre-process and clean the raw  sequencing reads  next step is the mapping of these reads  on the reference genome or the  transcriptome  thus the mapping tools will get  highlighted  here we are using bauti 2t  tool to map the reeds  bounty 2t  is a version of the bounty 2 algorithm  configured to run mapping on transcripts  defined in the gtf file  once you click on the bauti 2t option  you will get a pop-up with the ok option  click on ok will complete the mapping  once you are able to map your reads on  the reference genome next step is the  quantification of rna expression values  there are different methods for rna  expression quantification like sailfish  rsem htsec etc  here in our demo pipeline we are using  the rsem or rsemx  expression table method that will  produce an rna expression table with  fpkm value  the rsem stands for rna-seq using  expectation maximization that is a  software package for quantifying gene  and isoform abundances from single end  or paired and rnse data  thus click on the rsem exp table that  will be highlighted in a yellow color  our same exp table is a script that will  generate an expression table based on  the output of boutique 2t  the script is an adaptation of the rsem  algorithm by clicking on the rsim exp  table option you will get a pop-up with  the ok option  by clicking on the ok option you will be  able to quantify rna expression  once quantification of the expression is  completed next to complete the pipeline  you will need to check the end option  present on the top of the right side  of the interface  once you click on the end option you  will get a pop-up with ok  by clicking on the ok option you will be  able to complete your pipeline  as this is a demo pipeline the results  will be showcased on the spot  the output files labeled with the fbkm  contain expression measurements in fbk  whereas the other simply contain the  count of reads per g or isoform  the files labeled with not filtered txt  contain genes with zero expression for  all samples whereas those genes are  filtered out in the other files  recall from previous lesson that boutin  can output tables of the expression  levels of all genes or a table of only  those genes expression above zero for  most applications we will only be  interested in those genes with  expression above zero further it is  computationally much more expensive when  dealing with large data sets to open a  table including zero expression level  genes  therefore we will practice using the  table of only those genes with  expression  in other words a table in which genes  with expression is equal to 0 have been  removed besides iso from expression file  to look at isoforms  open the gene expression file to look at  the genes  to interpret the results obtained you  can visit the omex logic learn portal  and go through the course
 

